From 0dbf3df9376fd60121c125c5fb2df4ea9519a98b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sam <sam@example.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 20:11:56 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(tools): make text mode reliable for OpenAI-compatible
 providers

Rework the text/markdown tool protocol so it never depends on native tools: richer per-tool schemas and examples, ApplyPatch/AskQuestion/ChangeDirectory guidance, recursive argument validation and repair, markdown/JSON/XML parsers, and text-mode history that sends no tools key, no assistant.tool_calls and no tool roles (results are user tool_result blocks).

Also align CLI and VS Code tool names/arguments (Write/create_new_file, Edit/single_find_and_replace, Search/grep_search, List/ls, multi_edit), restore the session cwd on resume/fork, include a syntax+example reminder in tool error results, fix MCP prefixed tool lookup/readiness, and reduce VS Code webview freezes with incremental history windows and content-visibility.
